{% extends "layouts/docs" %}

{% block content %}
<p>This guide builds a small page with a shared layout. It takes a few minutes and assumes you have <a href="/docs/installation/">installed Kiln</a>.</p>

<h2>Create a layout</h2>

<p>A layout holds the markup every page shares. Each <code>block</code> marks a place a page can fill in. Save this as <code>templates/layouts/base.kiln</code>:</p>

{% apply highlight("kiln", title: "templates/layouts/base.kiln") %}
{% verbatim %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<title>{% block title %}My site{% endblock %}</title>
</head>
<body>
	{% block content %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<h2>Create a page</h2>

<p>The page extends the layout and fills its blocks. Save this as <code>templates/pages/home.kiln</code>:</p>

{% apply highlight("kiln", title: "templates/pages/home.kiln") %}
{% verbatim %}
{% extends "layouts/base" %}

{% block title %}{{ title }} | {{ parent() }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
	<h1>{{ title }}</h1>
	<ul>
		{% for feature in features %}
		<li>{{ feature }}</li>
		{% endfor %}
	</ul>
{% endblock %}
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<p><code>parent()</code> outputs the layout's version of the block, so the title becomes "Home | My site". The <code>.kiln</code> extension is optional in template names.</p>

<h2>Render it</h2>

<p>Create an environment that reads from the <code>templates</code> folder, then render the page with some data:</p>

{% apply highlight("ts", title: "render.ts") %}
{% verbatim %}
import { createKiln } from "@lucidcms/kiln";
import { fileLoader } from "@lucidcms/kiln/node";

const kiln = createKiln({
	loader: fileLoader({ root: "templates" }),
});

const html = await kiln.render("pages/home", {
	title: "Home",
	features: ["Fast", "Safe", "Familiar"],
});

console.log(html);
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<p>Kiln prints the full page. Lines that only hold tags, such as the <code>for</code> lines, are removed, so the output stays tidy:</p>

{% set layout %}
{% verbatim %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<title>{% block title %}My site{% endblock %}</title>
</head>
<body>
	{% block content %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
{% endverbatim %}
{% endset %}
{% apply example(source: false, name: "pages/home.kiln", templates: { "layouts/base.kiln": layout }, context: { title: "Home", features: ["Fast", "Safe", "Familiar"] }) %}
{% verbatim %}
{% extends "layouts/base" %}

{% block title %}{{ title }} | {{ parent() }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
	<h1>{{ title }}</h1>
	<ul>
		{% for feature in features %}
		<li>{{ feature }}</li>
		{% endfor %}
	</ul>
{% endblock %}
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<h2>Next steps</h2>

<ul>
	<li>Learn the <a href="/docs/language/syntax/">syntax</a> and <a href="/docs/language/expressions/">expressions</a>.</li>
	<li>Build reusable pieces with <a href="/docs/tags/component/">components</a>.</li>
	<li>Load data from templates with <a href="/docs/language/async-data/">async functions</a>.</li>
	<li>Add your own <a href="/docs/api/extending/">functions and filters</a>.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}
